f Albertus Institutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Career & Professional Development Mission for the Office of Career & Professional Development The Office of Career & Professional Development advances the mission of Albertus Magnus\n                                    College by assisting students and alumni in developing, evaluating and implementing\n                                    a career and professional development plan. As a division of the Office of Academic\n                                    Affairs, the Office of Career & Professional Development works collaboratively with\n                                    all areas of the College community and potential employers to enhance student and\n                                    alumni professional development. The following services will enhance your career development path while attending Albertus\n                                    Magnus College: Career Advising and Counseling Career Testing Internships Campus Recruitment and Interviewing Occupational Discovery and Job Shadowing Graduate and Professional School Planning Study Abroad Being an Entrepreneur Become Career-Ready with Internships Internship Success Stories: Garfield Robinson '23 Interning at the summer camp for All Saints Catholic Academy in New Haven was a homecoming\n                                             for this sports management major. As an alum of the school, Garfield was able to make\n                                             an impactful connection with the students. Watch Video Internship Success Stories: Arooba Sholmiyet '23 During her summer internship, business management and accounting major Arooba Sholmiyet\n                                             at Albertus helped solve real problems and create real budgeting solutions for a local\n                                             website designer. Watch Video Internship Success Stories: Jessica Reid '22 CVS Health accepts only the best of its internship applicants, but with her guidance\n                                             from Career Services, that was no problem for this healthcare management and accounting\n                                             double major. Watch Video Internship Success Stories: Amina Khokhar '22 This art management major never sees failure as an option. Her internship experience\n                                             at the Arts Council of Greater New Haven put that mindset to the test, and now, she\n                                             is #CareerReady. Watch Video Experiential Learning Events No events currently scheduled. Vision Statement Albertus Magnus College students and alumni will be empowered to pursue career and\n                                    professional development as a lifelong process. Start early on a path to career success with the solid foundation you will receive\n                                    at Albertus Magnus College. Visit the Office of Career and Professional Development\n                                    early on and throughout your time at Albertus Magnus College to discover how the Office\n                                    can help you develop realistic and flexible career goals that relate to your major\n                                    and future occupations. Learn the skills for lifelong career planning! Ready to start a conversation? Schedule an appointment with the Office of Career & Professional Development to see where your major can take you. Students and alumni can schedule an appointment through Handshake. The Office offers\n                                       both virtual and in-person appointments on Monday – Friday and has extended hours\n                                       each Tuesday until 6:30 pm. Meet the Staff Lisa Marotta Director of Center for Experiential Outreach Rosary Hall (Room 35) lmarotta@albertus.edu Sister Rosemary Reynolds, SNDdeN, MS, CAS Associate Director Rosary Hall (Room 34) rreynolds@albertus.edu (203) 401-4046 Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
    },
