gic Plan Profile of Albertus Institutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development All students and graduates are welcome to make an appointment with the Office of Career\n                                    & Professional Development. Albertus Magnus College's Office of Career and Professional\n                                    Development has a quick and effective way to schedule an appointment with staff members. The Office of Career & Professional Development is available to meet with students\n                                    (individually or in small groups), graduates, and alumni to improve career development\n                                    skills. The following is a sample list of services available: Career Advising and Counseling Career Testing Internships Campus Recruitment and Interviewing Occupational Discovery and Job Shadowing Graduate and Professional School Planning Study Abroad Being an Entrepreneur To schedule an appointment, log into Handshake and follow these steps: On the left navigation list, select “Career Center” and in the drop-down menu select\n                                       \"Appointments.\" Next, click \"schedule a new appointment.\" Select the \"Category\" (i.e., grade level)\n                                       and then select the \"Type\" of appointment from the list. Reserve an available appointment\n                                       slot, complete the \"pre-appointment survey,\" and then click \"Request.\" The Office of Career & Professional Development is open for appointments on Monday,\n                                    Wednesday, Thursday and Friday from 9:00AM - 4:00PM and on Tuesday from 9:00AM - 6:30PM Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Hours Available through Handshake for Virtual Appointment Monday 9:00am - 4:00pm Tuesday 9:00am - 6:30pm Wednesday 9:00am - 4:00pm Thursday 9:00am - 4:00pm Friday 9:00am - 4:00pm Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
