    "https://www.albertus.edu/student-resources/career-services/career-development-plan.php": {
      "title": "Career Development Plan",
      "description": "Career Development Plan at Albertus Magnus College Resources Veterans Employment Directory Give Campus Calendar Press Releases Proxy Access Commencement Centennial Celebration myAlbertus Search Menu Academics Back Undergraduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses International Students Transfer Students Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Graduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Student Resources Back Registrar Academic Support Services Accessibility Services Faculty Directory Falcon Fast Track Library Veteran's Educational Info Arts and Humanities Collaborative Admissions Back Undergraduate Back First-Year Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information Transfer Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information International Students Back Overview Apply for Admission International Student Services FAQs Tuition & Fees Live on Campus Virtual Tours Scholarships and Grants Visit Us Financial Aid Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Graduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Admission Requirements Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Resources Back Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Grants Falcon Fast Track Veteran & Military Search Courses Virtual Tours Parent Resources International Student Services About Back About Albertus Back Statement of Mission College History Catholic and Dominican Identity Multicultural Identity Office of the President Albertus Campus Back Meet Our Community New Haven Campus Campus Map Campus Video Tour News & Events Policies & Publications Back Overview Strategic Plan Profile of Albertus Institutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Career Development Plan The Student Success Roadmap provides a year-by-year plan with ways to make the most\n                                    of your academic and co-curricular experiences at Albertus Magnus College. Following\n                                    the Roadmap will also prepare you for a timely graduation and a successful career.\n                                    By taking these steps and using campus resources available to you, you will become\n                                    a part of a vibrant college community as you better yourself and society. First Year Participate in campus activities, join a club Meet with your Academic Advisor Check email, eLearning, and your grades daily Begin your Handshake Profile Complete the Focus2 Career Assessments Create your ePortfolio Attend the Service Fair & complete your service hours Attend the Major, Minor, & Albertus Grad School Fair Attend Career & Internship Fairs Have a professional photo taken Utilize the Writing Center, Math Tutors, and eTutoring Visit the Office of Career & Professional Development in Rosary Hall Attend a workshop sponsored by the Office of Career & Professional Development Explore Study Abroad Opportunities Sophomore Year Participate in Career Development Workshops Complete Professional Development Seminar Create your resume, cover letter, and a professional LinkedIn profile Attend the Service Fair Attend the Major, Minor & Albertus Grad School Fair Attend Career & Internship Fairs Begin to make plans for your Internship Update your ePortfolio Develop a long-term plan of classes with your Academic Advisor Continue to develop career readiness skills by being involved in school, community\n                                             & leadership positions Review summer jobs/internship opportunities Complete the Focus2 Career Assessments Secure your Internship & complete the paperwork on Handshake Junior Year Finalize your Internship, complete paperwork & evaluations on Handshake Attend the Service Fair Attend Career & Internship Fairs Update your ePortfolio Meet with a Career Counselor to review your resume/cover letter Shadow a professional in a career of interest Begin to develop your post-grad plans: graduate school or employment Continue to utilize on-campus academic resources Attend workshops & networking programs sponsored by Career & Professional Development Review summer job and internship opportunities Senior Year Update your resume, cover letter, & LinkedIn profile Complete your ePortfolio Complete a second internship if possible Consider a research project with a faculty member Attend Graduate School Workshop (if interested) Develop a plan for a job search Attend Career Readiness Workshops Attend Career & Alumni Office networking programs & mock interview opportunities Review jobs posted in Handshake Complete a Graduation Degree Audit Attend Career & Internship Fairs Finalize your post-grad plans: graduate school or employment Engage Albertus alumni on LinkedIn Set aside time weekly, to research job opportunities Inform Albertus Magnus College of your future plans Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Hours Available through Handshake for Virtual Appointment Monday 9:00am - 4:00pm Tuesday 9:00am - 6:30pm Wednesday 9:00am - 4:00pm Thursday 9:00am - 4:00pm Friday 9:00am - 4:00pm Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
