    "https://www.albertus.edu/student-resources/career-services/selecting-your-major.php": {
      "title": "Selecting Your Major",
      "description": "Selecting Your Major at Albertus Magnus College Resources Veterans Employment Directory Give Campus Calendar Press Releases Proxy Access Commencement Centennial Celebration myAlbertus Search Menu Academics Back Undergraduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses International Students Transfer Students Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Graduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Student Resources Back Registrar Academic Support Services Accessibility Services Faculty Directory Falcon Fast Track Library Veteran's Educational Info Arts and Humanities Collaborative Admissions Back Undergraduate Back First-Year Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information Transfer Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information International Students Back Overview Apply for Admission International Student Services FAQs Tuition & Fees Live on Campus Virtual Tours Scholarships and Grants Visit Us Financial Aid Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Graduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Admission Requirements Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Resources Back Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Grants Falcon Fast Track Veteran & Military Search Courses Virtual Tours Parent Resources International Student Services About Back About Albertus Back Statement of Mission College History Catholic and Dominican Identity Multicultural Identity Office of the President Albertus Campus Back Meet Our Community New Haven Campus Campus Map Campus Video Tour News & Events Policies & Publications Back Overview Strategic Plan Profile of Albertus Institutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Selecting Your Major Many times, students arrive at college unsure of what to major in, or they may change\n                                    their major over the course of their college years. It is important to check out the available undergraduate degree programs at Albertus\n                                    Magnus College. Students who are unsure of their college major should do the following: Explore online materials available Talk to professors about potential career opportunities Review the results of the career test given in your College Sucess Seminar course Reflect on interests, abilities, personality and values Speak to advisors about academic strengths and potential careers Schedule an appointment with a member of the Office of Career & Professional Development Get practical experience by doing an internship or volunteering in an interesting\n                                       field Additional Resources Online websites can also help you when making the decision on what to major in during\n                                    your time at Albertus Magnus College. The following is an additional resource that\n                                    can assist when choosing a major: What Can I Do With This Major? Ready to start a conversation? Schedule an appointment with the Office of Career & Professional Development to see where your major can take you. Students and alumni can schedule an appointment through Handshake. The Office offers\n                                       both virtual and in-person appointments on Monday – Friday and has extended hours\n                                       each Tuesday until 6:30 pm. Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Hours Available through Handshake for Virtual Appointment Monday 9:00am - 4:00pm Tuesday 9:00am - 6:30pm Wednesday 9:00am - 4:00pm Thursday 9:00am - 4:00pm Friday 9:00am - 4:00pm Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
