      "title": "Study Abroad",
      "description": "Study Abroad at Albertus Magnus College Resources Veterans Employment Directory Give Campus Calendar Press Releases Proxy Access Commencement Centennial Celebration myAlbertus Search Menu Academics Back Undergraduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses International Students Transfer Students Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Graduate Students Back Degree Programs Course Catalog Search Courses Academic Calendar Apply Request Information Student Resources Back Registrar Academic Support Services Accessibility Services Faculty Directory Falcon Fast Track Library Veteran's Educational Info Arts and Humanities Collaborative Admissions Back Undergraduate Back First-Year Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information Transfer Students Back Overview Apply for Admission Visit Us Request Information International Students Back Overview Apply for Admission International Student Services FAQs Tuition & Fees Live on Campus Virtual Tours Scholarships and Grants Visit Us Financial Aid Request Information Accelerated Adult Undergraduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Graduate Back Virtual Information Sessions Apply for Admission Admission Requirements Financial Aid Tuition Discounts Request Information Resources Back Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Grants Falcon Fast Track Veteran & Military Search Courses Virtual Tours Parent Resources International Student Services About Back About Albertus Back Statement of Mission College History Catholic and Dominican Identity Multicultural Identity Office of the President Albertus Campus Back Meet Our Community New Haven Campus Campus Map Campus Video Tour News & Events Policies & Publications Back Overview Strategic Plan Profile of Albertus Institutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Study Abroad Eligibility Requirements Paige Williams '20 Paige Williams studied abroad in London in 2019 and visited Barcelona during her semester. Albertus Magnus College administers study abroad programs and enforces study abroad\n                                    eligibility in a manner consistent with the policies and procedures described herein. Students (both first-time freshmen and transfer students) must complete two full semesters of study at Albertus Magnus College before going abroad and must achieve sophomore\n                                       standing prior to departure. Students must have a cumulative G.P.A. of a 3.0 or higher at the time of their application. Students must be in good academic standing and satisfactory academic progress toward a degree at Albertus. Students must not have participated in a prior study abroad experience in which financial aid money/Albertus Magnus College scholarship money was used to\n                                       pay for tuition and expenses. Students must participate in a Pre-Departure Orientation . Students must receive full approval for study abroad. Students cannot be in the last semester of senior year. Andrew Vitiello ‘25 Italy, 2024 Andrew spent his semester abroad visiting Italy. Albertus Magnus College reviews the disciplinary record s of all students seeking study abroad approval and determines their eligibility to\n                                    apply and participate in study abroad. Students on disciplinary probation are not\n                                    eligible to apply for or to participate in study abroad programs. They MUST have one\n                                    full semester, (fall or spring) on the Albertus Magnus College campus, with no additional\n                                    disciplinary incidents between the end of the probationary period and departure to\n                                    the host country. All students seeking approval for study abroad will have their records checked at\n                                    the time of application and the end of the term before the student’s departure to\n                                    receive final approval to study abroad. Program Selection Stephanie Santiago ‘25, France 2024 Stephanie Santiago studied abroad in France. Students interested in studying abroad through an Affiliate or Associate Program must\n                                          do the following prior to submitting an application directly to the program sponsor\n                                          or host institution: Attend a Study Abroad Info Session or meet with the Office of Career & Professional\n                                          Development to select an approved affiliate or associate program. Meet with their academic advisor to select courses from that program, which must provide\n                                          12 to 15 credits of coursework that will be applied directly toward their academic\n                                          degree. Study Abroad in Rome, Italy In Affiliation with Assumption University Study Abroad Anywhere in the World In Affiliation with the American Institute for Foreign Study Study Abroad in Dingle, Ireland In Affiliation with Sacred Heart University Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Hours Available through Handshake for Virtual Appointment Monday 9:00am - 4:00pm Tuesday 9:00am - 6:30pm Wednesday 9:00am - 4:00pm Thursday 9:00am - 4:00pm Friday 9:00am - 4:00pm Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
