nstitutional Effectiveness The Value of an Albertus Education College Resources Back Fast Facts Directory Faculty Employment Department of Public Safety Student Life Back Office of Residential Life Back Residential Life Residence Halls Meet the Staff Living on Campus Back Campus Hangouts Back Campus Video Tour Tab's Pub Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Falcon Campus Store Environmental Sustainability Dining Career Services Back Schedule an Appointment Undergraduate Students Back Four-Year Development Plan Selecting a Major Internship & Practicum Opportunities Study Abroad Graduate Students Back Career Development Workshops & Events Online Career Resources Handshake Student Resources Albertus Profile Accessibility Services Academic Support Services Back Academic Support Services Academic Advising Academic Support Center Research Support Services Health Clinic Back Overview Services Student Health Requirements Immunizations Counseling Services Back Students Suicide Prevention A Parent's Guide Dominican Ministries Meister Eckhart Center International Student Services Study Abroad Student Code of Conduct Technology Services Library Registrar Alumni Back Alumni Back Update Your Information Alumni Events Alumni Awards Back Overview Nomination Forms Past Recipients Golden Society From The Hill Publications Refer-a-Student Alumni Association Back Alumni Association Student Alumni Association Alumni Council Constitution & Bylaws Alumni Trustees Support Albertus Back Make a Gift Ways to Give Donor Recognition Societies Meet the Advancement Team Planned Giving Athletics Search: Online Career Links There are many outstanding resources online to help with career development, job searching\n                                    and interview preparation. The following is a sample list of online resources: CareerOneStop CareerOneStop is sponsored by the U.S. Department of Labor. A proud partner of the\n                                                   american job center network. Learn More DiversityJobs DiversityJobs is the #1 job board that unites diverse job-seeking professionals with\n                                                   employers who care about inclusive. Learn More Federal Occupational Search Learn More Getting Hired Getting Hired bridges the gap between job seekers with disabilities and employers\n                                                   looking to hire. Learn More G.I. Jobs G.I. Jobs is a link to military friendly employers. Learn More LinkedIn LinkedIn is a networking tool to find connections to recommended jobs, industry experts\n                                                   and business partners. Learn More JOB IN PSYCHOLOGY Learn More HOW TO HIGHLIGHT MILITARY EXPERIENCE ON YOUR RESUME Learn More CAREER RESOURCES FOR WOMEN IN TECH AND FINANCE Learn More HOW TO FIND CAREERS IN SUBSTANCE ABUSE TREATMENT & RECOVERY Learn More RESOURCES FOR HISPANIC AMERICANS IN THE WORKPLACE Learn More NACE Salary Calculator Learn More New York Times Jobs Learn More Zippia Zippia helps you find new career options and land a job now. Search by your major\n                                                   and see who would be interested in hiring you. Learn More Job Interview Questions Learn More Connecticut for Me for Young Professionals Learn More Jooble Job Search Learn More Landing Jobs in Top Tech Hubs Learn More Women in STEM Careers Learn More Careers in Social Work Learn More Cyber Security Education Guides Learn More NonProfit Career Network Search Learn More O*Net OnLine O*Net OnLine is a detailed description of careers used by job seekers, workforce development\n                                                   and HR professionals, students and researchers. Learn More How to Network in College Learn More Human Services Positions Learn More Public Health Career Guide Learn More Veterans’ Guide to Getting Hired Learn More ZipRecruiter Learn More Salary Calculator Resume Resources Adzuna Job Search Program Learn More Interview Advice Interview Advice reviews preparation, types, questions and competencies needed for\n                                                   a successful experience. Learn More Grad's Guide to Getting Hired Grad's Guide to Getting Hired explains how to deploy an effective search strategy. Learn More Landing Your Dream Job: Online Career Resources Landing Your Dream Job: Online Career Resources details how to find a career and future. Learn More A Student's Guide to Networking in College A Student's Guide to Networking in College explores timelines, tools and tips on making\n                                                   valuable contacts with your college. Learn More JobMesh Everything from entry-level jobs for students and jobs for international students\n                                                   without language skills to well-paid academic professions. Learn More Indeed Learn More Monster Learn More Simply Hired LinkedIn is a networking tool to find connections to recommended jobs, industry experts\n                                                   and business partners. Learn More InternWeb Learn More Albertus Magnus College LinkedIn Profile Learn More Resume Target The Office of Career & Professional Development at Albertus Magnus College has partnered\n                                                   with Resume Target to provide students with access to over 600+ resume templates by\n                                                   industry. To explore the FREE resume templates by industry visit Albertus Resume Templates\n                                                   to search the samples. Learn More Albertus Resume Templates Load More Career Links Career Services Career Development Workshops and Events Undergraduates Selecting Your Major Career Development Plan Falconship for Students Practica and Internships Should I Go to Graduate School? Study Abroad Career Development Resources Employment Tips Workforce Alliance Placement Success Record Career Development Workshops and Events Online Career Links Employers Overview Falconships for Employers Handshake Schedule an Appointment with the Office of Career and Professional Development Meet the Staff Alumni Services Falcon Flight to Career Readiness A Parent's Guide to Career Development Contact Office of Career & Professional Development careerservices@albertus.edu (203) 773-6989 Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 Hours Available through Handshake for Virtual Appointment Monday 9:00am - 4:00pm Tuesday 9:00am - 6:30pm Wednesday 9:00am - 4:00pm Thursday 9:00am - 4:00pm Friday 9:00am - 4:00pm Students Faculty Alumni Parents New Haven Campus Visit Transcript Requests Campus Map Calendar Library VA Benefits Support Albertus Directory Employment Policies & Reports Non-Discrimination Accreditation Title IX Albertus Magnus College 700 Prospect Street New Haven, CT 06511 (800) 394-9982 Contact Us Copyright © Albertus Magnus College, All Rights Reserved Website Privacy and Cookie Policy Copyright ©"
